.git
.github
.gitignore
log/*
tmp/*
storage/*
spec/
tests/
sorbet/
node_modules/
.bundle
.env*
README*
*.md
app/assets/builds/*
public/assets

# Deliberately NOT excluded: config/ai_private_keys.key and
# config/ai_private_keys.yml.enc (the AI Control Plane's AR-encryption key
# file and encrypted credentials). Unlike config/master.key /
# config/credentials/*.key — which are gitignored and never enter the build
# context at all, because RAILS_MASTER_KEY is supplied at runtime instead —
# ai_private_keys.key must be baked into the worker image, so it has to
# reach the build context via COPY . . in the `build` stage. Confinement to
# the worker happens in the Dockerfile (web-final copies from the
# `app-export` stage, which deletes the key before web-final ever sees it;
# worker-final copies from `build` unmodified), not here. Do not add an
# ignore rule for it — that would silently break the worker image instead.
